// How many SIGNIFICANT tokens two titles must share to be judged the same task.
// The breaker fires at a LOW count (park on the 3rd proposal), so it can't lean
// on the loop detector's 4-card volume gate to suppress a mis-group -- it must
// group precisely on its own. The detector's overlap-of-the-smaller-set test is
// too loose here: a short distinct title ("Review the Dev Mode PRD", tokens
// {dev,mode,prd}) shares 2 GENERIC tokens with the epics loop's seed and scores
// 67% overlap -> it would be falsely swept into the loop (the exact false-group
// the task warns against). Requiring >=3 shared SIGNIFICANT tokens kills that:
// the PRD card shares only the 2 generic UI words {dev,mode}; the real loop cards
// share {dev,mode,epics,html,artifacts,...} = 4-6. 3 specific words in common is
// a strong same-task signal; 2 generic ones is not. Cross-checked against the
// detector's own RT-12/RT-13 fixture (still groups: 4-6 shared) and its distinct/
// unrelated cards (0-2 shared -> never group).
