//     unattended; a human-gated task (deploy/push/delete/send/spend) is left in
//     `review` for the operator, never auto-run.
//   - review requires a DIFFERENT engine to approve before a task is `done`.
//   - SANDBOX GATE (the load-bearing one): only ENGINES THAT RUN SANDBOXED may
//     auto-EXECUTE a task. codex runs `--sandbox read-only`, so it cannot edit
//     files, run write commands, push, deploy, or exfiltrate. claude/hermes runs
//     have a full shell + the box's env (OAuth token, secrets), so a single
//     dispatched task -- however benign its title -- could push/deploy/curl the
//     token out. That is why claude/hermes autonomous runs are SANDBOXED: claude
//     now runs in the READ-JAIL (buildReadJail: chroot into an allowlist-only
//     root -- /home, /opt, all creds ABSENT -- plan mode, no Bash/net-tools),
//     which a 3-round red-team confirmed sound for the filesystem. codex runs
//     --sandbox read-only + the same jail. So claude + codex may auto-execute;
//     hermes has no read-only/tool-restriction flag and stays REVIEW-excluded.
//     Residual accepted by Steve (2026-07-18): the OAuth token in the child's own
//     /proc/self/environ is irreducible (inference needs it) + redaction is
//     transform-blind -- mitigated (plan-mode can't act, filesystem jailed), not
//     provably zero. Steve ratified adding claude to the exec set.
const AUTONOMY_FLAG = path.join(AGENTHOST_DIR, "autonomy.on");
const CHAINS_FILE = path.join(AGENTHOST_DIR, "chains.json");
