  // Object.prototype, so an ANONYMOUS request carrying `x-mesh-box:
  // constructor` (or __proto__, or toString) found a truthy "secret" in
  // meshReadAuthed, passed the guard, and threw inside crypto.createHmac --
  // and with no uncaughtException handler and no try/catch around the request
  // listener, that throw EXITS THE GATE. One unauthenticated request to
  // /mesh/identity took the whole box down: terminal, chat, Command Center,
  // phone view, and any agent turn in flight. Fly restarts it; the same
  // request kills it again. Verified locally 2026-08-01.
  // engine-sessions.js already uses this exact defence and says why.
  const safe = Object.create(null);
